WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.114 --> 00:00:01.147
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.147 --> 00:00:05.359
Today's message is Put
Things in Perspective.

00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:07.440
Over to you, Jean-Claude Biver.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.783
(rooster crows)

00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:12.148
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:12.148 --> 00:00:14.886
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:14.886 --> 00:00:18.469
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:19.378 --> 00:00:21.322
- When you have a down time,

00:00:21.322 --> 00:00:22.654
like if something didn't
work the way you want.

00:00:22.654 --> 00:00:23.907
- Yes.

00:00:23.907 --> 00:00:26.606
- What do you do to get
back on that positiveness?

00:00:26.606 --> 00:00:28.286
- I talk to the mountain.

00:00:28.286 --> 00:00:29.804
I have mountain next to my home

00:00:29.804 --> 00:00:31.700
that is called Rochers de Naye.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:32.753
It goes up to two.

00:00:32.753 --> 00:00:34.247
It's very low.

00:00:34.247 --> 00:00:37.247
It goes up to 2,004 or 2,005 meters.

00:00:38.279 --> 00:00:39.925
Or I talk to the Dents du Midi,

00:00:39.925 --> 00:00:42.802
which is 4,000 meters, which
is a little bit further away

00:00:42.802 --> 00:00:46.095
from my home, which I see every morning.

00:00:46.095 --> 00:00:48.058
I see those two mountains,

00:00:48.058 --> 00:00:50.148
and I say to these two mountains,

00:00:50.148 --> 00:00:54.321
mountains, I have a problem,
but when I look at you,

00:00:54.321 --> 00:00:56.486
you are 37 million old.

00:00:56.486 --> 00:00:57.873
(laughs)

00:00:57.873 --> 00:01:00.095
And I'm a little guy.
- You seem to be okay.

00:01:00.095 --> 00:01:01.488
- I'm a little guy here.
- And strong and tough.

00:01:01.488 --> 00:01:02.647
- We have a little problem.

00:01:02.647 --> 00:01:04.717
Can you help me?

00:01:04.717 --> 00:01:06.506
And the will say, come on.

00:01:06.506 --> 00:01:07.504
(laughs)

00:01:07.504 --> 00:01:11.179
Look, what we have already
seen in so many years.

00:01:11.179 --> 00:01:12.274
(laughs)

00:01:12.274 --> 00:01:14.807
Your problem is a nano problem.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.318
(laughs)

00:01:16.318 --> 00:01:17.151
Come on.

00:01:17.151 --> 00:01:19.037
Get up.
- Just get up. Do it.

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:20.112
- That's it.

00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:22.576
- Entrepreneurs do stupid things
when they lose perspective.

00:01:22.576 --> 00:01:25.386
People do stupid things
when they lose perspective.

00:01:25.386 --> 00:01:27.506
You make decisions that are
not in the best interest

00:01:27.506 --> 00:01:30.018
of your long-term self,
of the best version

00:01:30.018 --> 00:01:32.789
of yourself cause you're so
clouded by what's happening

00:01:32.789 --> 00:01:36.016
in the moment, and you
can't step out above.

00:01:36.016 --> 00:01:39.266
I may be the wrong target for this one.

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.208
I have a hard time with this message

00:01:42.208 --> 00:01:45.625
mostly because I don't get lost that much

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.824
in the day to day.

00:01:47.824 --> 00:01:49.244
I don't lose perspective that much.

00:01:49.244 --> 00:01:51.046
I think it's just more my personality.

00:01:51.046 --> 00:01:52.600
I don't get too highs with the highs,

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.817
and I don't get too low with the lows.

00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:56.514
I'm always constantly on stream, like,

00:01:56.514 --> 00:01:57.628
here's what we're trying to do.

00:01:57.628 --> 00:01:58.502
Okay, if there's a problem, great.

00:01:58.502 --> 00:02:00.892
Let's problem solve it, but
a problem in my business

00:02:00.892 --> 00:02:03.635
doesn't have to have a major
impact, for the most part,

00:02:03.635 --> 00:02:05.303
on how I feel about myself.

00:02:05.303 --> 00:02:06.516
And so we can get back on it.

00:02:06.516 --> 00:02:08.808
There's been maybe five days in my life

00:02:08.808 --> 00:02:13.141
where I've just been
so down or out or crazy

00:02:13.141 --> 00:02:15.513
that I lost perspective in
what I was trying to do.

00:02:15.513 --> 00:02:18.121
I think about when the
hardest day of my life

00:02:18.121 --> 00:02:20.872
when I told my business
partner that I quit.

00:02:20.872 --> 00:02:22.310
And it was just kind of in the moment,

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.986
frustrated, feeling out of control,

00:02:24.986 --> 00:02:27.209
feeling like I had no value to give,

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:31.934
feeling so worthless that
I made a rash decision

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:33.975
telling him that I quit.

00:02:33.975 --> 00:02:35.183
I didn't have the perspective.

00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:37.879
When I got up the next day,
and I went back to work,

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:39.799
I just realized I had to
find a different way to stay.

00:02:39.799 --> 00:02:40.994
And I realized it was still something

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.768
that I really cared about,
and so I don't really do

00:02:42.768 --> 00:02:44.509
a lot of things where I lose perspective.

00:02:44.509 --> 00:02:47.096
But I can understand for
others how it can be,

00:02:47.096 --> 00:02:48.520
I'm the weird one.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.367
I'm the crazy one.

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:51.967
I realize that's not most people.

00:02:51.967 --> 00:02:52.852
I think one thing though

00:02:52.852 --> 00:02:56.701
that can definitely help is gratitude.

00:02:56.701 --> 00:03:00.110
I think when you are grateful
for the things in your life,

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:02.270
you easily gain more perspective.

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:04.947
It's something that I have a
daily routine of and have had

00:03:04.947 --> 00:03:09.102
for years because it also
just makes me feel good.

00:03:09.102 --> 00:03:10.763
If you think about how fortunate you are

00:03:10.763 --> 00:03:12.777
even just to be watching this video,

00:03:12.777 --> 00:03:17.289
to have internet, to
have a house, to be fed,

00:03:17.289 --> 00:03:20.094
to live in an age where you have access

00:03:20.094 --> 00:03:22.666
to people who've done
things that you want to do

00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:24.866
and can learn from where 10 years ago,

00:03:24.866 --> 00:03:26.125
even, this didn't exist.

00:03:26.125 --> 00:03:27.954
Forget about what your grandparents

00:03:27.954 --> 00:03:29.797
or great-grandparents had access to.

00:03:29.797 --> 00:03:31.448
For the air that you get to breathe,

00:03:31.448 --> 00:03:33.076
you know, for the people in your life,

00:03:33.076 --> 00:03:35.990
for you just being a human
being instead of an ant,

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.483
you know, like, there's so many things

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.090
you can be grateful for.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.275
And just thinking about those things

00:03:41.275 --> 00:03:44.298
can make your problems seem a lot smaller,

00:03:44.298 --> 00:03:48.208
a lot less significant,
a lot less important,

00:03:48.208 --> 00:03:49.879
and that will allow you to then go off

00:03:49.879 --> 00:03:51.731
and do the right thing.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.805
So I would encourage you
if you ever feel like life

00:03:53.805 --> 00:03:56.493
is spiraling out of control,
one, try not to make

00:03:56.493 --> 00:03:59.009
any decisions when that's happening.

00:03:59.009 --> 00:04:00.776
Try not to make an important life decision

00:04:00.776 --> 00:04:03.281
by reacting quickly to something.

00:04:03.281 --> 00:04:05.514
Just hold your tongue, and sleep on it.

00:04:05.514 --> 00:04:08.148
And then, two, just try to think about

00:04:08.148 --> 00:04:09.516
what you can be grateful for.

00:04:09.516 --> 00:04:10.639
What is good in your life?

00:04:10.639 --> 00:04:13.342
There may be a lot that you
feel is terrible in your life,

00:04:13.342 --> 00:04:15.027
but compare it to most of the world.

00:04:15.027 --> 00:04:16.641
You've got it pretty good.

00:04:16.641 --> 00:04:19.210
And it's really hard to
be depressed and angry

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.976
and vengeful and hateful and spiteful.

00:04:21.976 --> 00:04:23.413
It's hard to hold those emotions

00:04:23.413 --> 00:04:26.305
at the same time as being grateful.

00:04:26.305 --> 00:04:28.718
And so if you can focus on your gratitude,

00:04:28.718 --> 00:04:31.056
and what you are really thankful for,

00:04:31.056 --> 00:04:32.171
they can help give you the perspective

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:35.054
you need to make the
best decisions for you.

00:04:35.054 --> 00:04:37.135
So the question of the day today is,

00:04:37.135 --> 00:04:38.725
this is what I do every day.

00:04:38.725 --> 00:04:39.628
I'm curious.

00:04:39.628 --> 00:04:41.790
Three things that you are grateful for.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.392
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:04:43.392 --> 00:04:44.524
Super curious to find out,

00:04:44.524 --> 00:04:46.473
and we will join in the discussion.

00:04:46.473 --> 00:04:48.318
