00:07:54.101 --> 00:07:54.934
- Oh, of course.

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:55.767
- [Graham] That one.

00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:56.600
The one we've heard about.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.887
- That one.

00:07:57.887 --> 00:07:59.993
The time I got caught, you mean.

00:07:59.993 --> 00:08:00.826
- Yeah, that one.

00:08:00.826 --> 00:08:02.081
(audience laughs)

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:03.597
Possibly it's the last time.

00:08:03.597 --> 00:08:06.806
(audience applauds)

00:08:06.806 --> 00:08:09.536
And see, this is the thing.

00:08:09.536 --> 00:08:10.872
This is the thing that amazes me.

00:08:10.872 --> 00:08:12.657
The way you talk about
it is your fantastic

00:08:12.657 --> 00:08:14.637
sort of unapologetic about it.

00:08:14.637 --> 00:08:16.162
And you didn't go into hiding.

00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:18.158
You didn't, you know, sort of go,

00:08:18.158 --> 00:08:19.648
you know, draw the curtains.

00:08:19.648 --> 00:08:21.538
Was it the next night you were out

00:08:21.538 --> 00:08:23.300
in a restaurant in LA having dinner?

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:24.133
- Absolutely.

00:08:24.133 --> 00:08:25.761
What's to apologize for?

00:08:25.761 --> 00:08:27.135
You know, I'm a gay man.

00:08:27.135 --> 00:08:29.977
At the time, I was like 36-years-old.

00:08:29.977 --> 00:08:32.085
Can I be, if I'm perfectly honest,

00:08:32.085 --> 00:08:33.839
if I'm perfectly, perfectly honest,

00:08:33.839 --> 00:08:37.682
outside of my career, I've
had a terrible run of luck

00:08:37.682 --> 00:08:39.279
that started about 10 years ago.

00:08:39.279 --> 00:08:42.133
I've watched a partner die.

00:08:42.133 --> 00:08:44.191
I've watched my mother die.

00:08:44.191 --> 00:08:48.358
I went, just after that, I
went to see a back surgeon

00:08:49.466 --> 00:08:52.244
who told that if I didn't
have two vertebrae removed

00:08:52.244 --> 00:08:53.535
